WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:03.302
-Our next guest is
an Oscar-nominated actor

00:00:03.302 --> 00:00:05.871
who stars in the Netflix series
"The Umbrella Academy."

00:00:05.871 --> 00:00:07.974
The third season
starts streaming June 22nd.

00:00:07.974 --> 00:00:09.175
Let's take a look.

00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:11.778
-Viktor,
we could go home tonight.

00:00:11.778 --> 00:00:13.412
Okay?
And for the first time in days,

00:00:13.412 --> 00:00:17.617
I'm feeling hope,
so please don't step on that.

00:00:17.617 --> 00:00:18.952
-Okay.

00:00:18.952 --> 00:00:20.486
Come on. We have to be
smarter about this.

00:00:20.486 --> 00:00:22.122
We don't know enough
about the Sparrows.

00:00:22.122 --> 00:00:24.023
-I've got you.
No one's gonna want to fight

00:00:24.023 --> 00:00:26.493
against me and
my tiny badass brother.

00:00:26.493 --> 00:00:29.062
-No more improvising, okay?

00:00:29.062 --> 00:00:31.263
We do things together
from now on. Got it?

00:00:31.263 --> 00:00:34.600
-Please welcome back to
the show Elliot Page, everybody.

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:36.736
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:36.736 --> 00:00:43.810 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:50.883 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:50.883 --> 00:00:51.784
Ahh.
-Hey.

00:00:51.784 --> 00:00:53.252
-Welcome back.
-How's it going?

00:00:53.252 --> 00:00:55.588
-This is a fantastic show

00:00:55.588 --> 00:00:59.592
about adoptive siblings
with superpowers.

00:00:59.592 --> 00:01:03.128
It's full of action.
The clip did not show that.

00:01:03.128 --> 00:01:05.965
I feel like this is
a very spoiler-laden show.

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:08.701
So when someone like you comes
on to do press, they give us

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:10.837
a clip that does not tell
much about the show at all.

00:01:10.837 --> 00:01:15.040
-Yeah, it's nice to keep it
exciting and full of surprises.

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:17.643
There's great twists and turns
this year.

00:01:17.643 --> 00:01:21.014
So -- And I think it shows
the balance of the show,

00:01:21.014 --> 00:01:23.383
and it's so fun to make
as an actor.

00:01:23.383 --> 00:01:27.720
It's so fulfilling as an actor,
and, yeah, we have so much fun.

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:30.890
-You also play violin
on the show.

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:32.558
Is this a skill
you had to teach yourself?

00:01:32.558 --> 00:01:33.927
Because it looks
very convincing.

00:01:33.927 --> 00:01:37.664
-I most certainly
did not teach myself,

00:01:37.664 --> 00:01:40.366
and I was pretty horrible at it.

00:01:40.366 --> 00:01:43.770
In my defense, they say it's
the most difficult instrument

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:47.473
to learn,
which I very much understand.

00:01:47.473 --> 00:01:49.041
[ Laughter ]

00:01:49.041 --> 00:01:52.178
But I had an amazing teacher
and a fantastic double.

00:01:52.178 --> 00:01:53.546
And I just...

00:01:53.546 --> 00:01:55.647
-That seems like --
-...did my best.

00:01:55.647 --> 00:01:58.351
-It seems like the second one
might be more helpful.

00:01:58.351 --> 00:02:02.088
-Yeah. She was fantastic.
Imogen. Incredible.

00:02:02.088 --> 00:02:04.823
So what a joy to listen
to her play on set.

00:02:04.823 --> 00:02:06.492
Me? [ Clicks tongue ]

00:02:06.492 --> 00:02:08.628
I'm sure the crew members

00:02:08.628 --> 00:02:12.031
were probably ready
to walk off set.

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:14.033
-Right.
So, since the show started,

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:17.537
you, as an actor,
came out as trans,

00:02:17.537 --> 00:02:21.007
and then your character
also came out as trans.

00:02:21.007 --> 00:02:23.843
Were these conversations that
you got to have with the writers

00:02:23.843 --> 00:02:25.611
about the journey
that your character took,

00:02:25.611 --> 00:02:28.614
having lived
that experience yourself?

00:02:28.614 --> 00:02:30.149
-Yeah, it was.

00:02:30.149 --> 00:02:33.819
And really with Steve Blackman,
the showrunner of "Umbrella,"

00:02:33.819 --> 00:02:38.591
who's just incredible
and such a wonderful person.

00:02:38.591 --> 00:02:40.993
And so, when we first
talked about it,

00:02:40.993 --> 00:02:46.031
he seemed really excited about
incorporating it into the show.

00:02:46.031 --> 00:02:51.303
And an incredible writer,
journalist, author

00:02:51.303 --> 00:02:54.173
Thomas Page McBee,
who I met doing a miniseries

00:02:54.173 --> 00:02:56.342
called "Tales of the City,"

00:02:56.342 --> 00:02:58.978
he wrote an extraordinary book
called "Amateur,"

00:02:58.978 --> 00:03:02.615
which I highly recommend
everybody to read.

00:03:02.615 --> 00:03:06.152
He was the first trans man
to box in Madison Square Garden.

00:03:06.152 --> 00:03:08.954
And his book
and his work in general,

00:03:08.954 --> 00:03:13.125
there's so much
about masculinity

00:03:13.125 --> 00:03:16.462
and what it means
and exploring that.

00:03:16.462 --> 00:03:21.066
So Thomas came on board
and helped out,

00:03:21.066 --> 00:03:23.235
and I feel proud of it

00:03:23.235 --> 00:03:25.905
and excited
for people to see it.

00:03:25.905 --> 00:03:29.275
-One of the nice things is,
your siblings on the show,

00:03:29.275 --> 00:03:32.077
when receiving the news
of the transition,

00:03:32.077 --> 00:03:34.280
are very supportive and loving.

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:36.015
Was this something that you had?

00:03:36.015 --> 00:03:40.252
I know you have run the gamut of
having to respond to reactions,

00:03:40.252 --> 00:03:41.821
both positive or negative.

00:03:41.821 --> 00:03:45.024
Were the people closest to you
in your real life

00:03:45.024 --> 00:03:47.459
as supportive
as the people on the show?

00:03:47.459 --> 00:03:49.995
-Yeah, absolutely. So --

00:03:49.995 --> 00:03:53.666
And I feel really grateful
for that. [ Laughs ]

00:03:53.666 --> 00:03:56.769
I think most people
weren't surprised or --

00:03:56.769 --> 00:03:59.339
It's something
I'd been talking about

00:03:59.339 --> 00:04:01.373
with a lot of people in my life.

00:04:01.373 --> 00:04:03.576
-I think that is
really important to know,

00:04:03.576 --> 00:04:06.846
which is -- So much
is being said about this issue

00:04:06.846 --> 00:04:08.981
from people who aren't
experiencing in real time

00:04:08.981 --> 00:04:11.183
or who don't know people
who go through it, right?

00:04:11.183 --> 00:04:12.752
If you know a loved one,

00:04:12.752 --> 00:04:15.021
this news probably comes
as less of a surprise

00:04:15.021 --> 00:04:19.425
than those of us on the outside
would expect it to be received.

00:04:19.425 --> 00:04:21.693
I know that since
you've come out as trans,

00:04:21.693 --> 00:04:24.364
you've had to receive,
you know, from the strangers,

00:04:24.364 --> 00:04:26.465
from people who don't know you
as a person,

00:04:26.465 --> 00:04:27.866
some pretty negative reactions.

00:04:27.866 --> 00:04:30.002
What has that journey
for you been like?

00:04:30.002 --> 00:04:31.704
-[ Chuckles ]

00:04:31.704 --> 00:04:36.375
Well, you know, what
I want to focus on right now

00:04:36.375 --> 00:04:38.945
and has been so extraordinary

00:04:38.945 --> 00:04:41.747
is the degree of joy
that I feel,

00:04:41.747 --> 00:04:44.750
the degree of presence
that I feel.

00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:49.221
I feel a way that I really
never thought possible

00:04:49.221 --> 00:04:51.490
for a long, long time.

00:04:51.490 --> 00:04:56.061
So that's really what I'm
focusing on embracing the most.

00:04:56.061 --> 00:04:59.465
But, of course,
moments can be overwhelming.

00:04:59.465 --> 00:05:01.067
Um...

00:05:01.067 --> 00:05:03.536
I feel like it's one of those
things where it's so unfortunate

00:05:03.536 --> 00:05:05.471
because it's like we're all
on the same team here.

00:05:05.471 --> 00:05:07.840
You know?
Whether you're trans, non-bin--

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:11.610
you know,
gender-nonconforming, cis,

00:05:11.610 --> 00:05:13.479
we all have these expectations

00:05:13.479 --> 00:05:16.449
and these sort of limits
and constraints

00:05:16.449 --> 00:05:19.251
because of, yes,

00:05:19.251 --> 00:05:21.520
sort of people's obsession

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:25.892
with, you know, the binary

00:05:25.892 --> 00:05:30.362
and how we're all
supposed to live our lives.

00:05:30.362 --> 00:05:33.299
So, you know, to me,

00:05:33.299 --> 00:05:38.037
it'd be so special for us
to all be able to connect

00:05:38.037 --> 00:05:41.974
and talk about how similar
we are in all of our journeys.

00:05:41.974 --> 00:05:44.710
-You wrote very beautifully
in "Esquire"

00:05:44.710 --> 00:05:46.679
about the joy you feel now

00:05:46.679 --> 00:05:50.416
and about how present you feel
in your body.

00:05:50.416 --> 00:05:53.886
Do you feel like that's
making you a better actor?

00:05:53.886 --> 00:05:56.489
I would imagine that
you had to get through so much

00:05:56.489 --> 00:05:58.457
to do a performance
in the past,

00:05:58.457 --> 00:06:03.262
and now it just must feel easier
to go out and do work.

00:06:03.262 --> 00:06:05.965
-It does, yeah. I mean,
everything does. You know?

00:06:05.965 --> 00:06:09.368
And that's obviously
a big component

00:06:09.368 --> 00:06:10.936
and part of my life.

00:06:10.936 --> 00:06:15.707
And, yeah, beautiful thing
to experience now,

00:06:15.707 --> 00:06:17.677
because a lot of the time,

00:06:17.677 --> 00:06:23.082
my life was just trying
to move forward.

00:06:23.082 --> 00:06:27.319
And so getting to embrace
the experience

00:06:27.319 --> 00:06:29.055
as much as I get to now.

00:06:29.055 --> 00:06:32.124
And I think it's made me
better in so many facets,

00:06:32.124 --> 00:06:36.529
like, as a person,
I think, as a friend,

00:06:36.529 --> 00:06:39.932
and, you know, relationships.

00:06:39.932 --> 00:06:41.601
-I think you both embrace it

00:06:41.601 --> 00:06:43.535
and you've probably
had it forced upon you

00:06:43.535 --> 00:06:45.170
to be an activist,
to some degree,

00:06:45.170 --> 00:06:47.172
about this
really important issue.

00:06:47.172 --> 00:06:49.742
And you've spoken about
how you want to approach it

00:06:49.742 --> 00:06:52.578
with empathy, which I think
is really beautiful

00:06:52.578 --> 00:06:56.248
and probably more effective.

00:06:56.248 --> 00:07:00.185
Do you find --
Does it come easy to you

00:07:00.185 --> 00:07:03.923
to approach this all
with empathy?

00:07:03.923 --> 00:07:05.892
-Not always. Um, but...

00:07:05.892 --> 00:07:08.093
[ Laughter ]

00:07:08.093 --> 00:07:09.962
I think --

00:07:09.962 --> 00:07:12.197
Yeah, I think, in some ways.

00:07:12.197 --> 00:07:16.902
And I think when you do --

00:07:16.902 --> 00:07:21.040
I reflect on certain
very difficult times in my life,

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:23.308
certain struggles
and obstacles and all that.

00:07:23.308 --> 00:07:26.446
And I think, ultimately
getting through that,

00:07:26.446 --> 00:07:28.847
I think it really
deepens your empathy.

00:07:28.847 --> 00:07:30.783
And I think of the times
in my life

00:07:30.783 --> 00:07:33.386
where I was
the most uncomfortable,

00:07:33.386 --> 00:07:35.555
where I was the most unwell

00:07:35.555 --> 00:07:37.856
are the times
when I was the most angry

00:07:37.856 --> 00:07:41.193
and I was the most unkind
to myself or self-righteous

00:07:41.193 --> 00:07:44.363
or all of those things.

00:07:44.363 --> 00:07:48.100
And so it's just --

00:07:48.100 --> 00:07:50.035
It's improved my life
drastically.

00:07:50.035 --> 00:07:52.738
And, um --

00:07:52.738 --> 00:07:55.808
And I hope, you know --

00:07:55.808 --> 00:08:00.079
I hope maybe people
who do have an issue with me

00:08:00.079 --> 00:08:03.415
can maybe try

00:08:03.415 --> 00:08:05.384
and hear that
and embrace that on some level.

00:08:05.384 --> 00:08:08.954
-Well, personally,
it is really lovely to hear

00:08:08.954 --> 00:08:10.589
how much joy it's brought you.

00:08:10.589 --> 00:08:12.925
And thank you so much
for sharing it with us

00:08:12.925 --> 00:08:15.694
and continuing to make it a
story other people can hear.

00:08:15.694 --> 00:08:18.464
Really nice to see you again.
-You too, Seth.

00:08:18.464 --> 00:08:19.832
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:19.832 --> 00:08:21.200
-Elliot Page, everyone.

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:23.135
The first season
of "The Umbrella Academy"

00:08:23.135 --> 00:08:25.705
starts streaming
June 22nd on Netflix.

